<title>SPAIN: EIB says new plan for Mediterranean ready soon.</title>
<headline>EIB says new plan for Mediterranean ready soon.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Investment Bank's (EIB) council of governors should soon formulate fresh plans to finance the Mediterranean southern region, EIB president Brian Unwin said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;We are really anxiously waiting for the council to make up its mind and decide the programme for the coming years,&quot; Unwin told journalists at a two-day forum of Mediterranean countries.</p>
<p>EIB is the main lender to Mediterranean countries which are not members of the European Union.</p>
<p>In the past year EIB lent these countries, mainly in northern Africa, around 1 billion ecu. But the amount of its budget dedicated to the region is low -- some three percent.</p>
<p>The EIB's council of governors is formed by the European Union's economy ministers.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, +341 585 8340</p>
